ts on ritual and language in order to develop a structure of rules in an economic and systematic way. These devices presuppose a spatial approach to ritual and language, one which deals for instance with absences as substitutions within a pre-existing grid, and not as temporal disappearances. In this way, the study reveals a key feature of some among the most influential schools of Indian thought. The sources are Kalpasūtra, Vyākaraṇa and Mīmāṃsā, three textual traditions which developed alongside each other, sharing - as the volume shows - common presuppositions and methodologies. The book will be of interest for Sanskritists, scholars of ritual exegesis and of the history of linguistics. - Cover."},"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-23T01:08:24.451887"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-06-11T00:39:13.297399"}}},"ISBN:9788178221793":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9788178221793","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9561070M/Eros_Consciousness_and_Kundalini","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9561070M/Eros_Consciousness_and_Kundalini","details":{"title":"Eros, Consciousness and Kundalini","subtitle":"Deepening Sensuality Through Tantric Celibacy and Spiritual Intimacy","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL232165A","name":"Stuart Sovatsky"}],"publish_date":"October 30, 2003","publishers":["New Age Books,India"],"weight":"1 pounds","physical_format":"Paperback","subjects":["Mind, Body, Spirit"],"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Going all the way,\" said Rick, dropping the phrase casually into our conversation."},"isbn_13":["9788178221793"],"isbn_10":["8178221799"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"9.4 x 7.3 x 0.5 inches","source_records":["amazon:8178221799","bwb:9788178221793"],"key":"/books/OL9561070M","number_of_pages":222,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL1935101W"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"identifiers":{"doi":["10.1604/9788178221793"]},